  "starterCode": "# Partial RoPE — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(x, positions, rotary_dim, theta=10000.0):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Partial RoPE** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, positions, rotary_dim, theta=10000.0):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    rotary_dim = int(rotary_dim)\n    if rotary_dim < 0 or rotary_dim > x.shape[-1] or rotary_dim % 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"rotary_dim must be even and within the last dimension\")\n    if rotary_dim == 0: return x.tolist()\n    head = x[..., :rotary_dim]\n    tail = x[..., rotary_dim:]\n    rotated = np.asarray(rope(head, positions, theta), dtype=float)\n    return np.concatenate([rotated, tail], axis=-1).tolist()\ndef rope(x, positions, theta):\n    import numpy as np\n    x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float); positions=np.asarray(positions,dtype=float); dim=x.shape[-1]\n    inv=1.0/(theta**(np.arange(0,dim,2,dtype=float)/dim)); ang=positions[...,None]*inv\n    c,s=np.cos(ang),np.sin(ang); out=np.empty_like(x)\n    out[...,0::2]=x[...,0::2]*c-x[...,1::2]*s\n    out[...,1::2]=x[...,0::2]*s+x[...,1::2]*c\n    return out\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
